  FIXTURE (SYNTHETIC, ISO-faithful): camt.054.001.08 ZKB-style collective-booking (Sammelbuchung).

  HONESTY NOTE. Like its zkb-shape-camt053-*.xml siblings, every value in this file is invented. It
  was hand-built (Datalink order types Z54/ZS4/ZQR) to the SIX Swiss Payment Standards Cash Management
  guidelines (camt.054.001.08, ISO MR 2019) and the ZKB Datalink shape, then validated well-formed.
  Every party, IBAN, reference and order id is a fixed fictitious test value; the amounts are the fact
  under test. A future shape change is modelled here with invented values too: fixtures in shipped
  paths are synthetic by construction.

  (This header names elements in prose without angle brackets on purpose: the regex parser scans the
  whole payload, so a literal tag token inside a comment would be miscounted as a real element.)

  WHAT THIS SHAPE PROVES (and camt.053 could not):
    - the real ISO 20022 notification element is Ntfctn (NOT the malformed Ntfcn an earlier parser
      revision looked for): a real camt.054 must be DETECTED as camt.054 at all.
    - ONE booked collective credit Ntry (the single line the bank also posts on the camt.053) whose
      NtryDtls carries a Btch header plus THREE TxDtls, one per underlying QR-bill payment: the D81
      fan-out is one bank_txn per TxDtls.
    - the three per-detail Amt (1500.00 + 2750.50 + 999.95) sum EXACTLY to the Ntry Amt (5250.45) to
      the Rappen: the parser's sum-check accounts for the whole collective booking or refuses it.
    - two details carry a 27-digit Swiss QR reference (QRR, under Tp/CdOrPrtry/Prtry) and one carries an
      ISO 11649 creditor reference (SCOR, RF..., under Tp/CdOrPrtry/Cd), each extracted from its detail.
    - camt.054 carries NO Bal element (SPS 2.3 p.53): opening/closing balances are absent, by design.

  If ZKB (or ISO) ever changes this serialization, these break. That is the point.
-->
